# L §4.2 last_business(p, n, cal) is "the n-th last business day of period p"; L §8.4 "a step or a count that isn't
# positive" is refused, here at the key (RUN-DOMAIN). Also a period with fewer business days than n (2026-03 under
# weekends [sat, sun] has 22): "a built-in's argument outside the domain its row states", RUN-DOMAIN. (Writer 8: was
# first_business's test; first_business is gone, L §2.2.)
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

input len: calendar
input n0: int
input n1: int
def c[m in months]: date = last_business(m, n0, len) at reader
def d[m in months]: date = last_business(m, n1, len) at reader

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  len = calendar(weekends [sat, sun])
  n0 = 0
  n1 = 23

ask q1: c[2026-03] law 2026-06-30
ask q2: d[2026-03] law 2026-06-30
=== expect
q1: refused: RUN-DOMAIN ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
q2: refused: RUN-DOMAIN ...
  law date 2026-06-30, cut 2026-12-31
